# thirdparty

Build third-party tools from source, then install them into the repo-local
default tool paths under `fecompiler/tools/*`.

Use a fixed build parallelism (`8`) to avoid saturating CPU resources.

## Build and Install (CPU-friendly)

```bash
cd /home/luyoung/ecc-fe

# 1) Slang: build + install to fecompiler/tools/slang
cmake -S fecompiler/thirdparty/slang \
      -B fecompiler/thirdparty/slang/build \
      -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
      -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/home/luyoung/ecc-fe/fecompiler/tools/slang
cmake --build fecompiler/thirdparty/slang/build --parallel 8
cmake --install fecompiler/thirdparty/slang/build

# 2) Verilator: build + install to fecompiler/tools/verilator
cmake -S fecompiler/thirdparty/verilator \
      -B fecompiler/thirdparty/verilator/build \
      -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
      -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/home/luyoung/ecc-fe/fecompiler/tools/verilator
cmake --build fecompiler/thirdparty/verilator/build --parallel 8
cmake --install fecompiler/thirdparty/verilator/build
```

## Quick Check

```bash
ls -l fecompiler/tools/slang/bin/slang
ls -l fecompiler/tools/verilator/bin/verilator
ls -l fecompiler/tools/verilator/bin/verilator_bin
```
